			"Message": "style(Mist): Normalise doc comments and fix indentation in WebSocket\n\nReplace hyphens with em-dashes in doc comments, remove redundant self-referential phrasing (\"This is useful for\" → \"Useful for\", \"will return\" → \"return\"), add missing `# Parameters` and `# Returns` sections to the `invoke` and `notify` methods, and fix the `ConnectWithSecret` method indentation that was double-tabbed.\n\nNo functional changes — documentation and formatting only.",
			"SHA": "c8c7bfee5886fd357d222dc9bca05ba7a7ca8ab2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:20:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mist): Implement WebSocket upgrade authentication and fallback dispatch\n\nAdd production-grade upgrade-time authentication to the local WebSocket server, completing the auth contract that was stubbed as a TODO. Native clients (Grove, Cocoon) present the per-spawn 32-byte shared secret via the `X-Land-Secret` header; browser clients (Sky) — which cannot set custom upgrade headers — authenticate via a `?secret=<hex>` URL query parameter or a `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` subprotocol entry (echoed back as RFC 6455 requires). A constant-time comparison function prevents timing side-channels on the credential check.\n\nThe `HandlerRegistry` also gains optional fallback dispatch: callers may register a `DefaultHandlerFn` via `RegisterDefault` that receives any unregistered method name alongside its params. This lets a single closure forward unknown methods into an existing dispatcher rather than exposing a hard error — critical for incremental migration where some callers still use an older JSON-RPC surface.\n\nTo avoid serialising concurrent connections on dispatch lookup, the handler map moves from `Mutex` to `RwLock` (read-dominated workload — one lookup per inbound frame, writes only at setup time). The `ServeLocal` signature relaxes `Secret` from mandatory to `Option<SharedSecret>` so callers that want loopback-only trust (no auth) can pass `None`.\n\nAcross all source files, doc comments are normalised: remove redundant self-referential phrasing (\"This function performs…\"), adopt consistent \"Builds\" / \"Provides\" verbs, and add `# Parameters` / `# Returns` sections to every public function.",
			"SHA": "abe0b5b5cc2e6257fd238e54a24f11f13cc28319"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T17:37:11Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Restructure README with Compatibility section, code formatting, and badge additions\n\nAdd a new Compatibility table documenting Mist's integration with Mountain, Air, Cocoon, and SideCar. Add Crates.io and Rust Version badges beneath the License badge for quick package visibility.\n\nApply consistent backtick formatting for proper nouns throughout the document (`editor.land`, `Node.js`, `JSON`, `gRPC`, `DnsPort`), bringing the README inline with sibling component conventions. Fix the mermaid diagram by removing doubled line-escape backslashes. Update the SideCar entry in the Integration table with its 🌏 emoji for visual consistency with adjacent rows.\n\nReorganise the Dependencies table by removing the Version column (versions drift vs. Cargo.toml) and retitling it to Key Dependencies. Restructure the blockquote quote attribution to sit directly under the emphasised line rather than in a nested paragraph. Correct the Project Structure tree by stripping the `Element/` prefix (Mist already is an Element) and adding a root `Cargo.toml` entry. Update the Vine reference emoji from 🍇 to 🌿 and bold the API Reference link. Add a CHANGELOG link to the Related Documentation section and remove the Project Maintainers footer.\n\nSource presentation and discoverability improvements only — no functional changes.",
			"SHA": "70f4ca5685e083742b20353d6cda80665a6e7fb9"
		},
