				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mist): Restructure README with features, architecture principles, and corrected doc URL\n\nRewrite and expand the Mist README to provide a more comprehensive overview of the DNS isolation component, matching the documentation depth of sibling components (Air, Mountain).\n\nKey changes:\n- Fix the Rust API Documentation URL from the generic `Rust.Documentation.editor.land/Mist/` to the correct project-specific `rust.documentation.mist.editor.land/`\n- Restructure the Overview with a clear problem-statement narrative explaining why Mist exists (DNS leakage prevention)\n- Add a dedicated 'Key Features' section covering Private DNS Zone, Forward Security, DNSSEC Signing, Dynamic Port Allocation, WebSocket Transport, and Loopback Binding\n- Add a 'Core Architecture Principles' table mapping principles (Network Isolation, Cryptographic Trust, Minimal Surface, Composability) to their key components\n- Add a 'Project Structure' directory tree showing the Source/, tests/, and Documentation/ layout\n- Extend the System Architecture mermaid diagram with a Connection Paths table documenting protocols and use cases for Mountain→Mist, Cocoon→Mist, Air→Mist, and Mist→External\n- Convert prose sections (Security Considerations, Getting Started, Dependencies) into structured tables\n- Replace the 'Funding' heading with 'Funding & Acknowledgements' and an emoji\n- Remove the trailing Security Policy link from the footer\n- Normalize em-dash separators (—) and consistent line wrapping across all sections\n\nNo functional changes — documentation and presentation only.",
			"SHA": "c9c5d1aa406522e2237278465c5b47556e1893ec"
